Source: dfw
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: dfw maintainers <lookap.dev@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), golang-go (>= 2:1.24~)
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: dfw
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: nftables, conntrack, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: docker-ce | docker.io
Description: firewall for the containers on chosen Docker networks
 dfw filters the traffic of the containers on the Docker bridge networks you
 name, in the kernel, on the ports of their bridges, with allow rules kept
 in /etc/dfw/rules. A new container is blocked from its first packet until
 its rules are in place, and a container no rule mentions has no network
 access. Other networks are left alone.
 .
 Installing the package activates nothing. Write the rules, run "dfw plan"
 to review them, then "dfw enable" to cut over.
